{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.conditional_fixed_strip","record":{"id":"scalar.conditional_fixed_strip","kind":"claim","label":"Formal fixed-strip implication with analytic hypotheses exposed","status":"unverified","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-fixed-strip","locator":"Processes/FiniteGaussianFixedStrip.lean:29–49; IsDiffusion.finite_gaussian_fixed_strip","statement":"In the SKValue model, for hX:IsDiffusion W gamma X and fixed 0<T<1, assuming GradientStrip T gamma.coeff (gradient W gamma) K L, nonnegative D,Lu,La, a uniform curvature bound D on [0,T]×R, time-space Lipschitz bounds Lu,La for gradient and curvature, and E curvature(t,X_t)²=1 for every t∈[0,T], the lemma proves eventual active-index normalizer positivity and the fixed-T shifted mesh limit.","assumption_ids":["scalar.fixed_strip_input_diffusion","scalar.fixed_strip_input_bounds","scalar.fixed_strip_input_unit_moment"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-conditional-fixed-strip"],"boundary":"The analytic bounds and moment identity are hypotheses of this lower-level implication. They are supplied within ContactAssembly for the top-level minimizer theorem; adding this source relation does not assert those inputs unconditionally."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.conditional_fixed_strip","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[],"direct_passages":[]},"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.conditional_fixed_strip&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.conditional_fixed_strip&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e3